\ ==== matrix div ====

\ element-wise matrix division by an all-nonzero divisor works
[ 4 6 8 10 ] 2 2 matrix  [ 2 3 4 5 ] 2 2 matrix  / .

\ a zero anywhere in the divisor is an error, matching the scalar path
[ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix  [ 1 0 2 2 ] 2 2 matrix  /
\ zero in the first cell
[ 1 2 ] 1 2 matrix  [ 0 1 ] 1 2 matrix  /

\ scalar divide-by-zero is also an error (existing behavior, shown for contrast)
6 0 /
\ scalar nonzero divide still works
6 3 / .

clear

\ ==== negate ====

\ scalar negate
5 negate .
-3 negate .
0 negate .

\ matrix negate is element-wise
[ 1 -2 3 -4 ] 2 2 matrix negate .
[ 5 -6 ] 1 2 matrix negate .

\ double negate is the identity
[ 1 2 3 ] 1 3 matrix negate negate .

\ negate on a non-numeric is a type error
"x" negate
[< 1 2 >] negate

clear

\ ==== inplace arith ====

\ In-place elementwise matrix arithmetic (+! -! *! /!): reuse the matrix
\ operand's buffer instead of allocating. A matrix operand is required.

\ matrix op scalar
[ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix 10 +! .
[ 10 20 30 40 ] 2 2 matrix 5 -! .
[ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix 3 *! .
[ 10 20 30 40 ] 2 2 matrix 10 /! .

\ scalar op matrix
10 [ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix +! .
100 [ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix -! .
4.0 [ 1 2 4 ] 1 3 matrix /! .

\ matrix op matrix (reuses the left operand)
[ 10 20 30 40 ] 2 2 matrix [ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix +! .
[ 10 20 30 40 ] 2 2 matrix [ 1 2 3 4 ] 2 2 matrix -! .

\ shape mismatch
[ 1 2 ] 1 2 matrix [ 1 2 3 ] 1 3 matrix +!

\ requires a matrix operand
5 3 +!

clear
